    "body": "Selecting a test case more than once in the comma-separated test_cases filter duplicates its workload, potentially scheduling the same training job repeatedly. Treat the selection as a set while preserving the workload order.\n\nValidation: three CPU selection regressions fail on the baseline and pass with the fix. Black, isort and Ruff passed. GPU training was not run.\n\nReview requested: @NVIDIA/mcore-oncall. This PR is ready for review with CPU regression evidence above. Upstream runner validation remains subject to NVIDIA contributor vetting.\n",
